course: dictionary
lesson: 2049
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word «conquer» is a good example. «In 1066 the Normans from France conquered England» means they took control of the country by fighting.
explain: The same word can be used in a different way. «She wanted to conquer her fear of water, so she joined the swimming club.» Here conquer means to beat a problem or a fear. Nobody was fought; the girl won against her own worry.
explain: Ask yourself: what is being conquered? A country, a mountain, a problem or a fear can all be conquered, and the clues in the sentence show you which meaning fits. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it.
fact: Conquer means to take control of a country or people by fighting.
fact: Conquer also means to beat a problem or a fear, or to climb to the top of a mountain.
fact: «Conquered» and «conquering» are other forms of conquer.
fact: A conqueror is the person who conquers, and a conquest is the act of conquering.
fact: «Divide and conquer» means to split enemies or a big problem into smaller parts so that each part is easier to beat.
exercise: «In 221 BC the king of Qin conquered all the warring kingdoms.» What does conquered mean here? | Forgave them | Became very popular with them | *Took control of them by fighting | Climbed to the top of them
exercise: «The band conquered America.» What does conquered mean here? | Stopped playing music | *Became very popular there | Took control of the country by fighting | Visited the country on holiday
exercise: Which word completes the sentence? «The Ottomans ___ Constantinople in 1453.» | conquering | *conquered | conquer | conquest
test: «After 1492 diseases helped the Spanish conquer the Aztecs and the Inca.» Which word means the same as conquer here? | *Defeat | Forget | Build | Visit
test: Mia says, «I will conquer my fear of the dark.» What does conquer mean? | She will sleep in the dark every night forever | She will climb a mountain at night | She will buy a torch | *She will deal with the fear and beat it
exam: Which sentence uses conquer to mean climb to the top of a mountain? | Toad conquered his fear of boats | *Lee conquered the mountain before lunch | The Normans conquered England in 1066 | The Romans conquered much of Britain
